[align=center]
[size=200][b]Support My Switch[/b][/size]
[color=#5B8DEF][i]Help Switch Vision support new hardware using privacy-processed real-device evidence[/i][/color]
[/align]
[hr]
Support My Switch is the preferred way to request support for new hardware, improve an existing model profile or provide diagnostic evidence.

[notice][b]Nothing is sent automatically.[/b]
Switch Vision prepares the contribution locally. You review it first, open the prepared email in your normal mail application and choose whether to send it.[/notice]

[size=150][b]What a contribution can contain[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]targeted or full SNMP walks
[*]Discovery reports and logs
[*]generated SNMP2MQTT configuration
[*]generated dashboard configuration
[*]device summaries and fingerprints
[*]model and validation information
[*]diagnostic evidence
[*]privacy reports
[*]optional contributor recognition
[/list]
You may also attach useful photos, screenshots or other evidence to the email.

[size=150][b]Privacy processing[/b][/size]
The contribution is built from a temporary copy. Your live Switch Vision data is not modified.
Credentials are always removed. Optional controls can mask management IP addresses, MAC addresses, hostnames, VLAN names and interface descriptions.

[warning]Full SNMP walks can reveal significant network inventory information. Always review a contribution before sending it.[/warning]

[size=150][b]Bundle quality[/b][/size]
[b]PASS[/b] — all included files were inspected and no blocking privacy condition was found.
[b]PASS WITH PRIVACY WARNINGS[/b] — the bundle was inspected but selected privacy options or detected content deserve additional review.
[b]REVIEW REQUIRED[/b] — something could not be safely inspected or sanitised. The prepared-email actions are withheld.

Review:
[code]BUNDLE_QUALITY.txt
SANITIZATION_REPORT.txt[/code]

[size=150][b]Creating a contribution[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Open [b]Switch Vision Hub[/b].
[*]Select [b]Support My Switch[/b].
[*]Choose privacy and recognition options.
[*]Select [b]Create contribution[/b].
[*]Review the result and device information.
[*]For an acceptable result, select [b]Prepare Email[/b].
[*]Switch Vision downloads a prepared [c].eml[/c] with the ZIP attached.
[*]Open it in your normal email application.
[*]Review the message and attachment.
[*]Press Send only when you are happy with what is being submitted.
[/list]

Send contributions to:
[code]switch-vision@zemerdon.com[/code]

[size=150][b]Recognition[/b][/size]
You can remain anonymous or choose a supported recognition identity. Private contributor details are not automatically converted into public attribution.

[size=150][b]What happens after sending[/b][/size]
Your contribution may be retained as original support evidence so model support, troubleshooting and future fixes can be reproduced and reviewed.
Where more testing is needed, follow-up should request only the minimum additional evidence required.

[size=150][b]Support levels[/b][/size]
[code]Detected → Experimental → Community Validated → Confirmed Supported[/code]
Real-device evidence is required for promotion. A generated profile by itself does not make hardware Confirmed Supported.
